2026-09-14 00:59 slice 34: struct methods + nested types + out/ref args + enum TryParse
- root cause of "struct ctors produce 0": ngen.zan Gen() collected methods only for
  AK.ClassDecl, so every struct had zero ctors (GenNew fell into the silent bare-alloc
  branch) and zero instance methods. Structs now collect like classes.
- nested type decls: ParseMember now dispatches class/struct/interface/enum members
  (it used to swallow the keyword into a garbage type ref), and FlattenNested hoists
  nested types to unit top level under their simple names, mirroring gen0's
  zan_parser_flatten_nested_types (recursion-first, order-preserving).
- out/ref arguments: parser keeps the full place expression (`out b.a`, `out arr[i]`,
  `out lst[i]`, `out Box.sv`); `out Foo x` declarations still parse as decl+name.
  ngen GenRefArg/AddrOf resolve real addresses (gen0 emit_ref_arg contract): frame
  slot, byref passthrough, this.field, static slot, member chains, array/List element
  with the same bounds guards as the stores. by-ref param slots are flagged (locRef)
  and every read/write/postfix goes through the pointer.
- EnumType.TryParse lowered in ngen (strcmp probe over the declaration-order member
  names; hit stores the constant through the out address, miss stores default(T)).
- ExprCls gained a MemberAccess case so field chains (x.next.n) resolve types.
